==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 15

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*5 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*4 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 113.33~120 seconds<sup>3,400f~3,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] spawns after 110 seconds<sup>3,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Angelic Beast Rajakong is the main pushing threat, so it is recommended to use Research [[Cat Combo]]s in combination with a level 40+ [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] to permanently stall it. Other than that, use [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and rusher-type units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] to whittle down Rajakong's health. Peons also come in waves in this stage, so bring long distance units such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to help stop the peon waves of Aku Doges and Ragin' Gories. The Kang Roos are free money, and the [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] will be shredded by Courier, so you likely only need to survive the 2 Gories and you're home free. If you also have [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] by now, the stage is made far easier.

